{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdsJ6reDw7YkJJPkHsgRM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four deliverables are written to the workspace root. Here's what I produced.\n\n**`clean_impl.py`** — a general encoder implementing exactly the four rules in `format.md`:\n- render each entry as `key=value`\n- join entries with `;`\n- escape `;` and `=` occurring in a value by prepending `\\`\n- nothing else (no key escaping, no backslash escaping, no reordering)\n\n**Undetermined behaviors** (exercised by probes, not pinned down by the spec):\n\n1. **Entry ordering.** `format.md` never states emission order. Probe `{\"b_key\":\"2\",\"a_key\":\"1\",\"c_key\":\"3\"}` is not sorted, so insertion order vs. sorted order diverge. I chose the dict's iteration order (insertion order).\n\n2. **Literal backslashes in values.** The spec mandates escaping only `;` and `=` and says nothing about `\\`. Probes `back`, `path`, and `msg` all contain literal backslashes. A reader worried about round-tripping could reasonably escape backslashes too; I followed the literal text and leave them untouched — so `\"\\\\\"` emits as a bare `\\`, and `\"escape \\; literally\"` becomes `escape \\\\; literally`.\n\nEverything else the probes touch **is** determined: value-only escaping of `;`/`=` (`tag=x\\=y`, `eq=\\=\\=`, `semi=\\;\\;`), and empty values (`{\"single\":\"\"}` → `single=`). No probe key contains a special character, so key-escaping — which the spec is also silent on — is not exercised and I did not list it.\n\nOne note on logistics: the two input files were located in an `inputs/` subdirectory of the workspace, not the root, so I read them from there; all outputs are written to the workspace root as specified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1957,"cache_read_input_tokens":33847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"e