{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":100190,"num_turns":14,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4568c4a9-9488-4e11-bd46-389680981455","total_cost_usd":0.39072599999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8718,"cache_read_input_tokens":233342,"output_tokens":7404,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8718,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":33847,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1957},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1625,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001705,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":7404,"cacheReadInputTokens":233342,"cacheCreationInputTokens":8718,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.38902099999999995,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-4-8","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All four deliverables are written to the workspace root. Here's what I produced.\n\n**`clean_impl.py`** — a general encoder implementing exactly the four rules in `format.md`:\n- render each entry as `key=value`\n- join entries with `;`\n- escape `;` and `=` occurring in a value by prepending `\\`\n- nothing else (no key escaping, no backslash escaping, no reordering)\n\n**Undetermined behaviors** (exercised by probes, not pinned down by the spec):\n\n1. **Entry ordering.** `format.md` never states emission order. Probe `{\"b_key\":\"2\",\"a_key\":\"1\",\"c_key\":\"3\"}` is not sorted, so insertion order vs. sorted order diverge. I chose the dict's iteration order (insertion order).\n\n2. **Literal backslashes in values.** The spec mandates escaping only `;` and `=` and says nothing about `\\`. Probes `back`, `path`, and `msg` all contain literal backslashes. A reader worried about round-tripping could reasonably escape backslashes too; I followed the literal text and leave them untouched — so `\"\\\\\"` emits as a bare `\\`, and `\"escape \\; literally\"` becomes `escape \\\\; literally`.\n\nEverything else the probes touch **is** determined: value-only escaping of `;`/`=` (`tag=x\\=y`, `eq=\\=\\=`, `semi=\\;\\;`), and empty values (`{\"single\":\"\"}` → `single=`). No probe key contains a special character, so key-escaping — which the spec is also silent on — is not exercised and I did not list it.\n\nOne note on logistics: the two input files were located in an `inputs/` subdirectory of the workspace, not the root, so I read them from there; all outputs are written to the workspace root as specified.","ttft_ms":4263,"ttft_stream_ms":3962,"time_to_request_ms":52,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":2503155,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"time_origin_ms":1786283936299.0115,"type":"result","duration_ms":100197,"uuid":"f543c097-62ac-43ea-baf9-b77066b28949"}
